{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ClimaxVolumeMass.NonSelfIntersectionProof","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ClimaxVolumeMass.NonSelfIntersectionProof","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.exclusionZone_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.exclusionZone_positive","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean#L113-L116","doc":"At `q > 1`, the exclusion zone has positive radius. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.hbarQ_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.hbarQ_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean#L109-L111","doc":"The exclusion radius vanishes in the classical limit `q → 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NonSelfIntersection.exclusionRadius_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NonSelfIntersection.exclusionRadius_pos","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean#L99-L107","doc":"**The exclusion zone is nonempty**: the radius is strictly positive.\n\nThis is what the free-field encoding could not give. Positivity is\nderived from the structure's own `q_gt_one`, through `hbarQ_pos`;\nno field of `NonSelfIntersection` asserts it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NonSelfIntersection.exclusionRadius_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NonSelfIntersection.exclusionRadius_eq","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean#L92-L97","doc":"The exclusion radius is exactly `ℏ_q` — now an unfolding lemma of the\ndefinition above rather than a projection of an assumed equation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NonSelfIntersection.exclusionRadius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NonSelfIntersection.exclusionRadius","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean#L76-L90","doc":"The exclusion radius of the quantum exclusion zone.\n\n**Derived, not carried.** The structure above used to have a free\nfield `exclusionRadius : ℝ` alongside a field\n`exclusionRadius_def : exclusionRadius = hbarQ q` asserting what it\nequals, and `exclusionRadius_eq` returned that second field — the\n§3b-cond item-5 degenerate shape, and this file's\n`proof-no-self-assuming-projection` ledger entry. A free field\nconstrained by an equation field is not a derivation: the radius could\nbe anything and the structure merely assumed it away.\n\nHere the radius is a definition of `q`, matching the library encoding\nin `QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean`, so it is not a free parameter at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NonSelfIntersection.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NonSelfIntersection.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean#L74-L74","doc":"`q > 1` — the non-classical regime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NonSelfIntersection.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NonSelfIntersection.q","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean#L72-L72","doc":"The deformation parameter `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NonSelfIntersection.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NonSelfIntersection.mk","kind":"ctor","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NonSelfIntersection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NonSelfIntersection","kind":"structure","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean#L62-L74","doc":"**Corollary: Obstruction to self-intersection.**\n\nFor `q ≠ 1`, the non-cocommutativity of the Hopf structure provides\nan energy barrier: the q-repulsion kernel diverges at `r = ℏ_q`,\ncreating a \"quantum exclusion zone\" of radius `ℏ_q = 1 − q⁻¹`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{cor:non-self-intersection}`\nRef: [freedman1994] https://doi.org/10.2307/2946567 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prf:non-self-intersection","label":"prf:non-self-intersection","md":"quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.quantumTwo_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.quantumTwo_pos","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean#L58-L60","doc":"The quantum integer `[2]_q` is positive when `q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.hbarQ_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.hbarQ_pos","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean#L54-L56","doc":"The quantum Planck constant is positive when `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qRepulsionKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qRepulsionKernel","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean#L46-L52","doc":"**q-Deformed repulsion kernel**.\n\nAt `q ≠ 1`, the classical `1/r²` kernel is replaced by\n`[2]_q / (r² − ℏ_q²)` which has a hard singularity at `r = ℏ_q`.\nRef: [freedman1994] https://doi.org/10.2307/2946567 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.quantumTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.quantumTwo","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean#L43-L44","doc":"The quantum integer `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean#L39-L41","doc":"The quantum Planck constant at a given (archimedean) substrate\nparameter value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean#L36-L37","doc":"The inverse indeterminate `q⁻¹` of `R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean#L33-L34","doc":"The canonical indeterminate `q` of `R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean#L29-L31","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}